# madcide keybinding profile: Emacs-style — the same action vocabulary
# as joe.keys respelled onto Emacs's CONTROL chords (C-x families
# included; the chord grammar is the same data joe's ^K uses).
#
# HONEST SUBSET (the two engine gaps, named): Meta has no key spelling
# yet (an ESC prefix cancels a pending chord), so the M- seats (M-v,
# M-w, M-x, M-g g) wait on a meta spelling; C-SPC (set-mark) has no
# NUL spelling, so the region pair is incomplete — mark stays unbound
# rather than squatting a fake seat. Region selection here is
# mark..caret live (no `bend` in this set), which IS the Emacs region
# model.
#
# File and exit
^x ^s save
^x ^c quit
^x ^f editfile
^x b editfile
# Buffers/project: C-x C-b (list-buffers) raises the project window.
^x ^b project
# Search
^s find
# Editing
^k delline
^w blockdel
^d del
^_ undo
# Movement
^a home
^e end
^v pgdn
# Repaint (C-l recenter's closest seat)
^l refresh
# Windows: C-x 2 / 1 / 0 / o — the direct Emacs seats.
^x 2 splitw
^x 1 onlywin
^x 0 killwin
^x o nextw
# The project window's keys (@project scope — profile data; the baked
# defaults add esc/backspace).
@project ins projadd
@project del projdel
@project enter projopen
